{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"The paired-copy kernel passed every workload and improves the large cases by roughly 2–3%. I have one verification run left. Before deciding whether to spend it, I’m checking one exact algebraic option: each 2×2, stride-2 transposed convolution has no overlap, so it can be expressed as a 1×1 convolution plus pixel shuffle. If ROCm preserves the accumulation order and executes it faster, it can remove more overhead without approximation."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport torch,torch.nn.functional as F\n\ndef alt(x,w,b):\n ci,co,_,_=w.shape\n ww=w.permute(1,2,3,0).reshape(co*4,ci,1,1).contiguous()\n bb=b[:,None].expand(co,4).reshape(-1).contiguous()\n return F.pixel_shuffle(F.conv2d(x,ww,bb),2)\ndef bench(fn):\n for _ in range(10):y=fn()\n torch.cuda.synchronize();s=torch.cuda.Event(1);e=torch.cuda.Event(1);q=[]\n for _ in range(50):s.record();y=fn();e.record();e.synchronize();q.append(s.elapsed_time(e))\n return sorted(q)[25],y\nfor B,H,ci,co in [(1,32,128,64),(8,64,128,64),(64,32,128,64),(1,256,128,64),(8,128,64,32),(1,512,64,32),(16,128,64,32)]:\n x=torch.randn(B,ci,H,H,device='cuda')*1e8;w=torch.randn(ci,co,2,2,device='cuda');b=torch.randn(co,device='cuda')\n t,y=bench(lambda:F.conv_transpose2d(x,w,b,stride=2));ta,z=bench(lambda:alt(x,w,b));d=(y-z).abs();print((B,H,ci,co),t,ta,t/ta,d.max().item(),(d/(y.abs()+1)).mean().item(),(d==0).float().mean().item())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
